Theorem CH-104: lattice engine bootstrap (L-7 idempotency on 2-dim sub-lattice)

  Preconditions:
    - s is an AimsState restricted to the Access x Consumption
      2-dim sub-lattice per Annex E §AIMS.1 + sec-1.2
    - Access carrier: Borrowed, Owned (height 1)
    - Consumption carrier: Dead, Linear, Affine, Unrestricted
      (height 3)
    - canonicalize_sub s is the canonicalization restricted to the
      Access x Consumption sub-lattice; CN-1 (Dead implies Absent)
      does not fire on this sub-lattice because Cardinality is
      excluded
    - lattice engine consumes per-dimension finite enumeration and
      explicit join-table verification per the foundational-axiom policy
      sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape
    - L-7 idempotence claim: canonicalize_sub
      (canonicalize_sub s) is equal to canonicalize_sub s

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in (Access x Consumption).
      canonicalize_sub (canonicalize_sub s) is equal to
      canonicalize_sub s;
      i.e. canonicalization is idempotent on the
        Access x Consumption sub-lattice (L-7 restricted form).

  Proof obligation:
    Per-dimension finite enumeration over the 8 states of the
    Access x Consumption sub-lattice. For each state, exhibit
    canonicalize_sub once and twice; verify equality.

      State (Borrowed, Dead):
        canonicalize_sub once: no CN rule fires on this sub-lattice
          (CN-1 requires Cardinality; CN-8 requires Locality);
          result is (Borrowed, Dead).
        canonicalize_sub twice: same; idempotent.
      State (Borrowed, Linear):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Borrowed, Linear).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Borrowed, Affine):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Borrowed, Affine).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Borrowed, Unrestricted):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Borrowed, Unrestricted).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Owned, Dead):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Owned, Dead).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Owned, Linear):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Owned, Linear).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Owned, Affine):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Owned, Affine).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.
      State (Owned, Unrestricted):
        canonicalize_sub once: no rule fires; result (Owned, Unrestricted).
        canonicalize_sub twice: idempotent.

    Closed-world coverage:
      8 states exhibited; each verified canonicalize_sub once and
      twice; idempotence holds in all 8 cases. Per L-9 (SCALAR
      sentinel excluded), SCALAR is not a state on the sub-lattice
      and is excluded from this enumeration.

    Join-table verification:
      Per-dimension join is max on a totally ordered carrier; the
      join-table over the 8 states is symmetric and idempotent
      (max(a, a) = a). The sub-lattice's product join is the
      componentwise dimension join; idempotence of the product
      follows from idempotence of each dimension (L-3 restricted
      form).

    Lattice validation:
      L-7 (canonicalize idempotent) is restated for the sub-lattice
      and discharged by the 8-state finite enumeration above. The
      restricted form composes monotonically with L-7 on the full
      7-dim lattice when the excluded dimensions (Cardinality,
      Uniqueness, Locality, Shape, Effect) are at their idempotent
      identity (the CN rules on those dimensions are themselves
      idempotent per L-7 on the full lattice).

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension finite enumeration; explicit join-table
               verification; idempotence claim discharge)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
